  {
    "number": 160,
    "title": "Add Pixoo general controls to the BUNNY component view",
    "body": "The BUNNY component view exposed only Monitor/Media and monitor settings for Pixoo, although the Pixoo controller already declares screen power, brightness and media on controller v1. This adds those general controls to the same view under ADR 0005. Refs #151.\n\nScreen power, brightness, saved-playlist selection and the six declared playback actions appear in the Pixoo view and work without an observed session. Each control submits one guarded controller v1 command through the existing hub route with the snapshot's request ticket, configuration revision and generation. Availability follows the declared capability, the credential's control scope and the Pixoo mode; every disabled control names the missing capability, scope, stale evidence or mode. Playlist and playback controls are disabled in Monitor or while a mode change is pending, with a one-click explicit \"Switch to Media\" through the mode control. No command changes the mode as a side effect, nothing restores automatically, and uncertain results stay locked until the user loads current values. Playlists are listed by ID until Pixoo #67.\n\nOne recorded reassessment: Pixoo `main` c81bc31 declares controller v1 modes unsupported and accepts Monitor/Media only through its integration extension, while the delivered fixture declared v1 modes. The Pixoo mode control and the explicit switch now use the integration `mode` operation, and the fake Pixoo declares the real capabilities. Nanoleaf still declares only Work/Quiet/Free, so its general controls render disabled with reasons until Nanoleaf #64 and #153.\n\nScope: `apps/dashboard` source, fixtures, browser scenarios and evidence; a hub test that general commands are validated and scoped before any controller request; dashboard, development, architecture and README notes; OpenSpec change `gh-151-pixoo-general-controls` with the `unified-dashboard` delta. The hub route, controller v1 contract and Pixoo extension are unchanged. No hook, installation, agent session, state migration or device operation. Physical acceptance is #154.\n\nAcceptance evidence at 8790d51 on Node 24.13.0: `npm run build`, `npm run typecheck`, 6 dashboard unit tests, the full browser suite and the nine-scenario matrix (four new #151 scenarios: guarded commands in Media with keyboard submission, Monitor gating with the explicit switch and a pending mode, concurrent edits with a typed conflict and a locked uncertain action, read-only and undeclared reasons with axe at desktop and 390px), 71 hub tests, 19 setup tests, the reproducible hub package, hub MCP, workflow checks, and the unchanged contract, lifecycle, agent-state and MCP suites in both languages. The `generalReasons` unit test and the matrix scenarios failed before the UI change and pass after it. Committed receipts are under `apps/dashboard/evidence`; screenshots stay outside Git.\n\nRisk: incorrect commands can change what the display shows. Bounded by schema validation before forwarding, the controller's revision and generation guards, per-device serialization, typed conflicts and locked uncertain results. Transport receipts are never presented as physical results.\n\nRemaining completion work: independent Standards and Specification reviews of the frozen comparison, all six current-head CI jobs, explicit human approval of the actual UI candidate under the SDLC UI approval scope (screenshots delivered to the owner; renewed after any UI change), the work-guide entry, OpenSpec sync and archive, guarded squash merge, merged-main CI readback and issue closure.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
    "state": "open",
